    <task><title>Part a</title>
<statement><p>In terms of <m>a</m>, <m>f</m>, and <m>h</m>, give the coordinates of points <m>P</m> and <m>R</m>.</p>
<p><m>P</m> has coordinates <m>(</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>,</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/><m>)</m>.</p>
<p><m>R</m> has coordinates <m>(</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>,</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/><m>)</m>.</p>
</statement><answer><p><m>a+h</m></p></answer><answer><p><m>f\mathopen{}\left(a+h\right)</m></p></answer><answer><p><m>a</m></p></answer><answer><p><m>f\mathopen{}\left(a\right)</m></p></answer></task>
    <task><title>Part b</title>
<statement><p>In terms of <m>a</m>, <m>f</m>, and <m>h</m>, give the lengths of the legs of this right triangle.</p>
<p><m>PQ</m> has length <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0005"/>.</p>
<p><m>QR</m> has length <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0006"/>.</p>
</statement><answer><p><m>h</m></p></answer><answer><p><m>f\mathopen{}\left(a+h\right)-f\mathopen{}\left(a\right)</m></p></answer></task>
    <task><title>Parts c and d</title>
<statement><p>Give a formula, in terms of <m>a</m>, <m>f</m>, and <m>h</m>, for the slope of the line through points <m>P</m>
and <m>R</m>.</p>
<p>Slope =
<fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0007"/>.</p>
<p>Recall that the average rate of change of a function <m>f</m> on the interval <m>[a,a+h]</m> is defined by the formula <me>AV_{[a,a+h]} = \frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h}.</me>
How is the slope of the line through the points <m>P</m> and <m>R</m> related to this average rate of change of <m>f</m>?</p>
</statement><answer><p><m>\frac{f\mathopen{}\left(a+h\right)-f\mathopen{}\left(a\right)}{h}</m></p></answer></task>
